<center><font face="arial"><b>MEETING THE NEIGHBORS</b></center>
<hr size="2" color=<%=color1%>>

Jim White (IDFG), Denny Dawes (WHI), Peter Goodwin (UI), and Scott Wasem (ISWCD), and Linda Klein (LRK) met with our upstream neighbors, the Gibler family, on July 9th at Don and Sara Jo Johnson's home located on the Gibler property.  Sara Jo is a Gibler.  Other Giblers attending were Gene (Ned's son), Dick, Stephanie (Jim's daughter), Fred and wife Margaret, Russ (Fred and Margaret's son), Nancy (Fred and Margaret's daughter), and Scott McLeod (Berta's son).
<p>
The Giblers pieced together some history of the meadow by recalling stories from their childhood.  We answered some of their questions about our restoration project on the WMA.  The Giblers gave us permission to do some topographic and monitoring surveys on their property this fall.
<p>
Thank you, Gibler family, for a great afternoon - it was certainly nice to meet all of you!

